// Task 6 pilot (G5): framed literally, as `"Sacrifice this permanent"` — the
// escape clause ("no parseable frame reproduces this wording") does not
// apply here, only to `~`, below. `"Sacrifice this permanent"` compiles
// cleanly with zero holes at `FragmentKind::Cost` (corroborated three ways:
// `crates/deckmaste_english/src/fragment.rs:405` already uses the sibling
// `"{2}{W}, Sacrifice this artifact"` as a clean `Cost` fixture; `permanent`
// is a `noun_count` in `crates/deckmaste_english/regular-vocabulary.tsv:
// 589`; and `cargo xtask english bracket "Carnival Elephant Meteor"`
// brackets it as a real cost constituent). Not vacuous data either: 13
// corpus cards print this literal wording (Acidic Sliver, Basal Sliver,
// Carnival Elephant Meteor, the Sliver cycle, Ygra).
//
// What's still open: `"Sacrifice this permanent"` itself covers only
// 12/1575 (0.8%) attestations of "Sacrifice this <TYPE>" in the supported
// corpus — the other 99.2% need "this creature"/"this artifact"/etc.
// instead. No hole in the current frame compiler models "this <the invoking
// card's own type>" — the hole-constituency audit's own §4.3 remedy (a
// non-param, card-level binding source for a hypothetical `<This>` hole) is
// not built, so this literal frame is real but narrow: it matches/renders
// exactly one of the many type-specific wordings, not a general one.
//
// The obvious *parameterized* candidate — `frames: ["Sacrifice ~"]` — was
// also authored and compiles cleanly (a `HoleClass::SelfRef` hole), but is
// the WRONG tool and was NOT adopted: `~` resolves structurally to
// `NounPhrase::ThisCard`, which has exactly two forms
// (`ThisCardForm::{FullName, AbbreviatedName}`,
// `crates/deckmaste_english/src/syntax/phrase.rs:62-78`), both rendering as
// the card's own printed NAME (`crates/deckmaste_english/src/renderer.rs:
// 920-921`) — never as a type-generic demonstrative. The legacy `template:`
// renderer's own `~` handling agrees: `'~' => out.push_str(subject)`
// (`crates/deckmaste_cards/src/render/template.rs:45`), where `subject` is
// the invoking card's name. Concretely: this macro is invoked live by
// `plugins/builtin/tokens/{Clue,Gold,Treasure,Food,Blood}.ron`, so rewriting
// the checked-in `template:` to `"Sacrifice ~"` (the only way to make G2
// agree with a `~`-framed authoring) would flip their rendered cost from
// "Sacrifice this artifact" to "Sacrifice Clue"/"Sacrifice Gold"/etc. — a
// real regression, not a hypothetical one. See
// `docs/superpowers/research/2026-07-30-macro-frames/
// pilot-constituency-findings.md` for the full finding.
(
    name: "SacrificeThis",
    template: "Sacrifice this permanent",
    kinds: [CostComponent],
    frames: ["Sacrifice this permanent"],
    body: Do(Sacrifice(This)),
)
